            <ToolValue Name="SubmissionComments">v1.4, September 26th, 2026. A.S.Borlaff - NASA/ARC
- Resubmission with APT 2026.4.3.
- Updating the pointings with new approximate date for observations. Assuming 2026-10-28T00:00:00.0
- Build with ROSALIA 1.3.2 - beta 'mosaic_tests' 390f0ff1bb062e373607cded53488f800ca92112


v1.3, June 18th, 2026. A.S.Borlaff - NASA/ARC
- Resubmission with APT 2026.4. No changes from 1.2. 

v1.2: June 5th, 2026. A.S.Borlaff - NASA/ARC
- Automatic updating of coordinates and APT based on ROSALIA/WFS: https://rosalia.readthedocs.io/en/latest/commissioning.html
- ROSALIA now uses exposure class instead of rosalia_stray method. Bug fixed that led to a several arcmin mismatch of the WFICEN in the simulated exposures. 

v.1.1: April 3rd 2026, A.S.Borlaff - NASA/ARC 
- PAV3 bug fixed. RA DEC PAV3 calculated for Dec 1st, 2026. 

v.1.0: April 3rd 2026, A.S.Borlaff - NASA/ARC 
- WARNING: All the observations in this APT require specific V3PA angles. There is a discrepancy between the internally calculated V3PA angles and the scheduling windows calculated by the APT. This is being investigated in the Roman HelpDesk INC022</ToolValue>
